---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../../../components/Hero.astro';
import Cta from '../../../components/Cta.astro';
import SectionNav from '../../../components/SectionNav.astro';
---
<Base title={"Six Situations Community Banks Bring Us on Problem Hotel Loans"} description={"Unfunded improvement plan, franchise default, maturity default, payment default, receivership, and OREO: what the bank is weighing in each, and what we look at."}>
  <Hero eyebrow="For community banks" title={"Six situations, and what the bank is weighing in each."} lead={"These are the problem hotel loans we are asked to look at. In each, what the bank is deciding and what helps."} />
  <SectionNav section="communityBanks" />
  <main id="main">
    <section class="section" id="situation-1"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Situation 01</p><h2>Unfunded improvement plan</h2><p>The brand has required renovations the owner cannot pay for, and the flag is at risk.</p></div>
      <div class="cells">
        <div><h3>What the bank is weighing</h3><p>Whether the flag is worth saving, who would fund the work, whether the bank advances new money to do it, and how much time the brand will give.</p></div>
        <div><h3>What we look at</h3><p>The scope, cost, and deadline of the plan, the brand's position, and the comfort letter. We value the hotel twice: once with the plan done and the flag kept, and once as an independent or reflagged hotel. The lower-risk figure sets our basis.</p></div>
        <div><h3>What to have ready</h3><p>The improvement plan, correspondence with the brand, the latest quality inspection, and the owner's plan to pay for the work.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div></section>
    <section class="section alt" id="situation-2"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Situation 02</p><h2>Franchise default</h2><p>The brand has issued a default or termination notice for unpaid fees or failed inspections.</p></div>
      <div class="cells">
        <div><h3>What the bank is weighing</h3><p>Whether to cure the default, what the comfort letter allows, and how long the cure period has to run. A hotel that loses its flag loses much of its demand.</p></div>
        <div><h3>What we look at</h3><p>The notice and the cure deadline, the fees owed, and whether the bank's rights with the brand pass to a buyer of the loan.</p></div>
        <div><h3>What to have ready</h3><p>The notices, the comfort letter, the fee statements, and the inspection results.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div></section>
    <section class="section" id="situation-3"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Situation 03</p><h2>Maturity default</h2><p>The hotel is operating, the loan has matured, and a refinance will not cover the balance.</p></div>
      <div class="cells">
        <div><h3>What the bank is weighing</h3><p>Another extension, a discounted payoff, or a loan sale. The gap between the principal balance and what a refinance would lend, and what the appraisal says now.</p></div>
        <div><h3>What we look at</h3><p>The T-12, the debt service coverage, the appraisal, and what the owner has done to refinance.</p></div>
        <div><h3>What to have ready</h3><p>The appraisal, the T-12, any refinance quotes the owner has received, and the payment history.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div></section>
    <section class="section alt" id="situation-4"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Situation 04</p><h2>Payment default</h2><p>Revenue has fallen below what the hotel needs to cover debt service.</p></div>
      <div class="cells">
        <div><h3>What the bank is weighing</h3><p>Whether the shortfall is temporary or structural, and whether a forbearance agreement would buy time that is actually useful.</p></div>
        <div><h3>What we look at</h3><p>The trend in RevPAR against the comp set, who manages the hotel, and whether taxes, payroll, or vendors are being deferred.</p></div>
        <div><h3>What to have ready</h3><p>Monthly performance reports, tax filings, and an aging of payables, if the bank has them.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div></section>
    <section class="section" id="situation-5"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Situation 05</p><h2>Receivership</h2><p>A receiver is operating the hotel while the bank decides between selling the loan and foreclosure.</p></div>
      <div class="cells">
        <div><h3>What the bank is weighing</h3><p>The receiver's costs, how long the case will run, and any protective advances already made.</p></div>
        <div><h3>What we look at</h3><p>The order of appointment, the receiver's reports, any sale procedures already approved, and the status of the foreclosure. We can purchase the loan with the receivership in place.</p></div>
        <div><h3>What to have ready</h3><p>The order, the receiver's reports, and a ledger of advances.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div></section>
    <section class="section alt" id="situation-6"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Situation 06</p><h2>Closed or OREO hotel</h2><p>The hotel has gone dark, or the bank has taken title and wants to sell.</p></div>
      <div class="cells">
        <div><h3>What the bank is weighing</h3><p>The cost of carrying a closed hotel: taxes, insurance, security, and deferred maintenance, while the staff, the licences, and the flag fall away.</p></div>
        <div><h3>What we look at</h3><p>The condition of the building, the franchise status, the licences and permits, and the liabilities that remain.</p></div>
        <div><h3>What to have ready</h3><p>The appraisal, the condition and environmental reports, tax and insurance status, and any licence correspondence.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap"><div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Related reading</p></div><ul class="toc"><li><a href="/banks/what-we-buy/">What we buy <span>Banks</span></a></li><li><a href="/library/pip/">Pricing a hotel loan with an unfunded improvement plan <span>Library</span></a></li><li><a href="/library/receivership/">Keeping a hotel open through receivership <span>Library</span></a></li><li><a href="/blog/foreclosure-timelines-and-hotel-value/">Foreclosure timelines and why they matter more for hotels <span>Blog</span></a></li></ul></div></section>
  </main>
  <Cta title={"Discuss a hotel loan in confidence."} text={"A conversation and an indicative price carry no obligation to sell."} label={"Start a conversation"} />
</Base>
